 - |\n\n  Line 98: The phase is planned and no build has started, so every criterion is unmet. The operator answered every design question on 2026-11-12 and kept the CARRY-003 rows AC-015 to AC-017. No code task starts before phase 007's before-measurement is confirmed done.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/plan.md:\n  Line 39: - [x] The operator keeps the CARRY-003 group (\"Carry three, settle five (Recommended)\").\n\n  Line 107: Setup records the before numbers, the live brief heads, the reach check, the hook timing and the suite. Implementation waits for the phase 007 confirmation, then runs the waves in `tasks.md`: the table, the fields, the head, the degraded contract, the reach check, the tests, the id retirement, the `nm-sk-doc-01` fix and the CARRY-003 group. Verification rebuilds, reruns every floor, the CLI checks, the brief heads, the reach check with real embeddings and the suite, then fills the summary.\n\n  Line 172: The operator answered the four design questions on 2026-11-12, each with the recommended option: \"Rename the four, drop /prompt (Recommended)\", \"Only a typed command (Recommended)\", \"The strictest: ask (Recommended)\" and \"No (Recommended)\". The same day the operator kept CARRY-003 in this phase, moved the `nm-sk-doc-01` fix here (\"Fix it in phase 005 (Recommended)\") and set phase 007's before-measurement first (\"Now, on today's branch tip (Recommended)\"). `spec.md` section 10 holds each answer.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/spec.md:\n  Line 40: **Scope Boundary**: The public recommendation fields, the hook brief head, the degraded-path contract, the allow-list retirement and the hand-authored bridge leftovers. Scoring, the policies themselves, `AGENTS.md` and the runtime pointers stay as they are. The group labelled CARRY-003 holds three criteria phase 003 left unmet and can be kept or dropped as one unit.\n\n  Line 204: - CARRY-003: clear the typed `/create:agent` ambiguity, prove that a metadata command with no compatibility row is active and reach `/speckit:search` from the review's probe prompt.\n\n  Line 236: | `ADV/lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json` | Modify | CARRY-003 (a) and (c) |\n\n  Line 237: | Tests under `ADV/tests/` | Create, Modify | Schema, golden briefs, degraded contract, old daemon, CARRY-003 (b) |\n\n  Line 273: ### CARRY-003 - Criteria phase 003 left unmet (keep or drop as one group)\n\n  Line 277: | REQ-015 | CARRY-003 (a): the default command capture prints `[]` for `typed_same_owner_ambiguous`, with the pinned numbers unchanged. |\n\n  Line 278: | REQ-016 | CARRY-003 (b): `scoring-compatibility.json` lists no `command-spec-kit-plan`, `-complete`, `-implement` or `-resume` row, and a fixture test proves that a metadata command with no compatibility row is active in both runtimes. |\n\n  Line 279: | REQ-017 | CARRY-003 (c): `show me which packets mention the token cap` returns a passing entry with `command` `/speckit:search` and `policy` `run`, with false offers still 0 of 35. |\n\n  Line 308: | Risk | The CARRY-003 (a) fix changes ambiguity for other prompts | Med: the ambiguity count moves | The pinned capture is the gate, and the fix is reverted and marked blocked if it moves |\n\n  Line 310: | Risk | The CARRY-003 (c) phrase is written for a known probe prompt | Med: it scores that prompt and little else | The tune reach and false-offer counts must hold, and the group can be dropped as one unit |\n\n  Line 365: - Does CARRY-003 stay in this phase? Decision: yes, by the earlier answer \"Carry three, settle five (Recommended)\". Phase 003's ADR-017 points at this group.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/work