em-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/advisor-quality-049-003.vitest.ts\"},\"output\":\"commit 1c80022452b8748399e3c581e83217532f7bfcee\\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <82775228+MichelKerkmeester@users.noreply.github.com>\\nDate:   Tue Oct 27 11:10:13 2026 +0100\\n\\n    fix(system-skill-advisor): stop calling a confidence floor or a held skill a tie\\n    \\n    The advisor flagged 110 of 261 labelled routing prompts as ambiguous,\\n    mostly because the task-intent confidence floor lifts unrelated skills\\n    to 0.82, within the 0.05 confidence margin of a top that earned its\\n    confidence. A floored skill now clusters on the score margin alone when\\n    the top is not floored, and a skill the typed-command bound held below\\n    a command's owner records that owner as heldBelow and never clusters\\n    with it. The brief uses the scorer's ambiguity answer and names a real\\n    cluster member after \\\"vs\\\", and the low-information abstention still\\n    reads the wider cluster so a floored skill cannot top an\\n    under-specified prompt.\\n    \\n    Over the 261 prompts, flags fall from 110 to 78 with the same 202\\n    correct top skills and no top skill changed; the typed\\n    /deep:research :auto prompt now reads ambiguous false. Released as\\n    system-skill-advisor 0.17.7.0. Also keeps /specs/other/ local.\\n    \\n    Spec: system-speckit/054-weak-model-spec-authoring/024-typed-command-ambiguity\\n    Commit-Id: 0012433\\n\\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts b...\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/scratch/logs/w0b-T055.out:\n  Line 3: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1794522385627,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2e22251effedzgdgxW9ZYGzGw\",\"part\":{\"partID\":\"prt_1d1de89e3001h9tZ1f5BCF