{"type":"text","timestamp":1794530659676,"sessionID":"ses_e2dad3a2dffe46l7KA6EEh2b1G","part":{"id":"prt_1d25cb760002fntA9u1J5mr7Ol","sessionID":"ses_e2dad3a2dffe46l7KA6EEh2b1G","messageID":"msg_1d25cb13a001GcmKcxHAJjboN3","type":"text","text":"**T044 complete.** Checkbox left unticked.\n\n## Files changed\n\n1. `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts`\n   - In `clustersWithTop`, once the score gap exceeds `AMBIGUITY_MARGIN`, a member carrying `confidenceFloored` now returns `false` instead of falling through to the confidence margin. This covers both cases: the top is not floored (prior behavior) and both are floored (new rule), so two floored candidates cluster on the score margin alone. The wide-abstention path (`applyFloorException=false`) is unchanged.\n   - Updated the module comment to state the durable reason.\n\n2. `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/advisor-quality-049-003.vitest.ts`\n   - **Deviation, required by the task's own Verify:** the existing test `clusters the same pair when the top cleared a floor too` asserted the exact opposite of the requested rule (both floored at confidence 0.82 with a 0.36 score gap expected ambiguous). I renamed it to `does not cluster two floored candidates whose scores are outside the margin` and flipped the assertion to `false`. Without this, `npx vitest run tests/scorer` cannot report 0 failed. No other test lines changed.\n\n## Verify output\n\n```\n$ cd .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime && npx vitest run tests/scorer\n RUN  v4.1.12 /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime\n\n Test Files  37 passed (37)\n      Tests  348 passed | 2 skipped (350)\n   Start at  01:43:03\n   Duration  8.15s\nvitest_exit=0\n```\n\n```\n$ node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'\n[159,50,20,5]\nexit=0\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- I did not rebuild `dist` (T044 does not name a build, and T046 does it). `$P` therefore read the build made by T057, before this source edit. The change cannot move ranking: it only alters `ambiguousWith`/`ambiguous`, and the low-information abstention path calls `wideAmbiguityMembers` with `applyFloorException=false`, which is untouched. T046's rebuild is the authoritative post-change metric run.\n- No other files touched, no git state changed, no checkbox ticked.","time":{"start":1794530654048,"end":1794530659676}}}
